{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Symptom\n\n`_metered_spend()` in `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` accumulates token spend across regions, but a single CloudWatch `ClientError` returns `None` from lines 316-318 or 329-331, discarding totals already collected from healthy regions.\n\n## Code facts from `origin/main`\n\nBoth cited paths resolve under `origin/main`: `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` and `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`.\n\n`_metered_spend()` builds per-region CloudWatch queries at lines 283-315, prices token data into `total` at lines 332-337, returns `0.0` when no per-model series exists at lines 338-340, then returns `total` at line 341. The only production call site is `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py:477`.\n\n`handler()` consumes the result at the CE-poll trigger on line 493, unavailable handling at lines 507-514, display/log text at lines 523-540, the release guard at line 562, and the attach path at line 570. Existing tests already cover whole CloudWatch listing failure returning `None` at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:357-367` and whole data failure returning `None` at `:370-394`. They do not cover a later-region failure after a healthy region contributes a partial total. The current `FakeAWS.client()` returns the same CloudWatch fake for every region at `:176-187`, so partial-region tests need a region-aware CloudWatch fake.\n\nOther `_metered_spend` references found in `origin/main`: monkeypatch helpers at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:249` and `:254`; direct unit calls at `:363`, `:390`, `:433`, `:889`, and `:919`.\n\n## Sequencing after 604c-ade8\n\nThis ticket is sequenced after sibling ticket `604c-ade8`, which is already certified, claimed, and touching the same handler file first. That plan removes the unconditional `metered is None` CE-poll trigger from line 493. It keeps only the due interval plus near-threshold metered-spend triggers so a metered outage cannot override `CE_MIN_INTERVAL_SECONDS`.\n\nCfe0 must not reintroduce `metered is None`, `metered.degraded`, or any equivalent unconditional degraded-meter trigger at line 493. A degraded partial must not force the near-threshold branch merely because it is degraded; that would recreate the per-tick CE hammering that 604c removes. The post-604c gate should stay conceptually `due or (metered is not None and metered_total * 5 >= THRESHOLD_USD * 4)`, with cfe0 adapting `metered_total` to `MeteredSpend.total`.\n\nThe arithmetic risk is explicit: `MeteredSpend.total` is a lower bound, so the near-threshold test can be false while full regional spend would be true. That is the trade-off created by 604c's interval policy. Cfe0 handles it by carrying `degraded=True` into release safety and operator visibility: degraded partials block release, expose the failed regions, still attach when the observed partial reaches the cap, and rely on the due CE interval for the next authoritative read.\n\n## Design\n\nUse a small result object, not a bare float: `MeteredSpend(total: float, degraded: bool, failures: tuple[MeteredFailure, ...])`, where each `MeteredFailure` stores `region` and `exception_class`. If at least 1 token series contributes before or after a regional `ClientError`, return `MeteredSpend(total=<partial>, degraded=True, failures=...)`. If no token series contributes before a CloudWatch `ClientError` prevents a complete scan, keep the unavailable path by returning `None`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py` defines `MeteredSpend`.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.total` stores the numeric CloudWatch dollar total.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True` when at least 1 region raises `ClientError` during the scan.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed region name.\n- [x] `MeteredSpend.failures` stores each failed exception class.\n- [x] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `list_metrics`.\n- [x] `_metered_spend()` returns a degraded `MeteredSpend` after one region contributes token spend then a later region raises during `get_metric_data`.\n- [x] `_metered_spend()` continues scanning later regions after an earlier region raises `ClientError`.\n- [x] When a CloudWatch `ClientError` prevents a complete scan before any token series contributes, `_metered_spend()` returns `None`.\n- [x] Degraded-region logging includes the failed region name.\n- [x] Degraded-region logging includes the exception class name.\n- [x] The CE-poll gate uses `MeteredSpend.total` for near-threshold arithmetic.\n- [x] A degraded partial below the near-threshold amount does not poll CE before the due interval.\n- [x] A degraded partial at the near-threshold amount polls CE before the due interval.\n- [x] The CE-poll gate contains no unconditional `metered.degraded` trigger.\n- [x] The CE-poll gate contains no unconditional `metered is None` trigger reintroduced by cfe0.\n- [x] `signal_unavailable` is `True` when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [x] A degraded partial with `total >= THRESHOLD_USD` attaches the deny policy when it is not attached.\n- [x] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` leaves an existing deny policy attached.\n- [x] A degraded partial with `total < THRESHOLD_USD` publishes no release notification.\n- [x] Metered log text reports the numeric partial total when `MeteredSpend.degraded` is `True`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` extends `FakeAWS.client()` so CloudWatch fakes can vary by `region_name`.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_listing_fails` covers the listing-failure partial.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_preserves_partial_total_when_later_region_data_fails` covers the data-failure partial.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers region name logging.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_records_degraded_region_failure` covers exception class logging.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_below_near_threshold_respects_ce_interval` covers the non-due no-poll case.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_at_near_threshold_polls_ce` covers the near-threshold poll case.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_can_attach` covers fail-closed attachment.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_degraded_partial_meter_cannot_release` covers release blocking.\n- [x] `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py::test_metered_spend_cloudwatch_failure_before_any_series_reports_unavailable` covers the `None` fallback.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` exits 0.\n- [x] `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify` exits 0.\n\n## Testing\n\nDuring development, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py -k 'metered_spend or degraded_partial_meter'`. Before push, run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py`, then `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make verify`.\n\n## Source\n\nRaised from Gerrit change 2984 patchset 7 review feedback, then narrowed to preserve partial CloudWatch totals without weakening 604c's CE polling interval or release safety.\n\n## Verification evidence\n\nVerified against merged commit `1f338f2c57e7235ac9410829d685e5ea249f0b8c` (Gerrit change 2997, tip of `origin/main`) in a throwaway detached worktree, so no uncommitted local edit could influence the result.\n\n- `MeteredSpend` is defined at `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/handler.py:288` with `total` (289), `failures` (291) and the `MeteredFailure.exception_class` field (284).\n- The degraded construction is `handler.py:371`: `MeteredSpend(total=total, degraded=bool(failures), failures=tuple(failures))`.\n- Both region-scan failure paths log and then `continue` (`handler.py:344-346` for `list_metrics`, `357-359` for `get_metric_data`), so a later region is still scanned.\n- The pre-contribution failure path returns `None` at `handler.py:367-368`.\n- Degraded-region logging carries both the region and the exception class at `handler.py:301-303`.\n- The CE-poll gate is `if due or near_threshold:` at `handler.py:535`, with `near_threshold` derived from `metered.total` at `533-534`. It contains no bare `metered.degraded` disjunct and no bare `metered is None` disjunct, so the unconditional trigger that `604c-ade8` removed has not been reintroduced.\n- `signal_unavailable` incorporates `metered.degraded` at `handler.py:565-568`; fail-closed attachment is `621-623` and release requires `not signal_unavailable` at `608`.\n- `FakeAWS.client()` varies the CloudWatch fake by `region_name` at `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py:169-186`.\n- All 9 named tests exist and assert the behaviour claimed, at lines 432, 472, 515, 697, 719, 773, 790 and 1389.\n- `pytest tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` → `61 passed in 16.26s`.\n- `make verify` passed in CI: Gerrit change 2997 carried `Verified +1` before it was submitted, and `Verified` runs the gating `ubuntu-latest, py3.13` cell that `make verify` mirrors locally."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789890748324958209,"uuid":"66d4f8f9-ce95-43b6-bc0f-810efc63139f"}